  "id": "DrugBank_DB00595 - MONDO_1195",
  "verbalization": "Oxytetracycline appears to be linked to Spotted Fever through a chain of indications that involve typhus and relapsing fever. The evidence suggests that Oxytetracycline is associated with Typhus, which in turn is linked to both Chloramphenicol and Demeclocycline, both of which are indicated to treat Spotted Fever. This implies a potential pathway where Oxytetracycline may exert some therapeutic effect on Spotted Fever through indirect mechanisms involving these related antibiotics. The presence of multiple indirect pathways supports the idea that Oxytetracycline could be repurposed for Spotted Fever, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these indications highlights the importance of considering related antibiotics in the context of disease treatment and repurposing.",
